TOTK: a mesh shader as a compute kernel, for a GPU without VK_EXT_mesh_shader (the job's "as_compute": n,
MeshStage.AsCompute; runtime/vk_exec_draw.c mesh_emulate). One workgroup a meshlet runs the stage as the mesh entry
point does and writes into the runtime's emulation buffer, through a 64-bit address the module holds as two marker
constants the runtime replaces: the draw's VkDrawIndexedIndirectCommand, the vertices (position, then each generic
attribute in location order, a vec4 each) and the triangles' indices, which an indexed draw with a pass-through vertex
shader then reads. A triangle past the meshlet's count, or naming a vertex past its last, is degenerate. A task shader
as compute keeps each task workgroup's payload and launch count in the buffer and writes the dispatch of the mesh
kernel, whose workgroup (j, t) runs launch j of task t and takes a meshlet slot from a counter. Triangles only, without
per-primitive attributes (Program.cs refuses the rest). Without the field every translation is as before.

